    "result_text": "All tests pass. The build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `customerCode` assignment (`<LAST3>-<NNNN>`) for `POST /api/owners`:\n\n**Domain & persistence**\n- `Owner.java` \u2014 added a `customerCode` field (`@Column(name = \"customer_code\")`) with getter/setter.\n- `db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql` \u2014 added a nullable `customer_code` column to the `owners` table.\n- `db/hsqldb/data.sql` \u2014 extended the positional seed inserts with the new column value (`NULL`), so DB init still matches the widened table. (h2/postgres use explicit column lists, so they were unaffected.)\n\n**API contract**\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 added a read-only `customerCode` property to the `Owner` schema. This regenerates `OwnerDto` with the field, so MapStruct maps it automatically and `GET /api/owners/{id}` returns it.\n\n**Request pipeline** (OfficeFloor function injection, per AGENTS.md)\n- New function `AssignOwnerCustomerCode` \u2014 takes the built `@Val Owner` and `OwnerRepository`, builds `LAST3` from the upper-cased first three letters of `lastName`, and sets `NNNN = findAll().size() + 1` zero-padded to 4 digits.\n- `owners.POST.yml` \u2014 inserted an `assignCode` step between `build` and `save`, under `govern: [ transaction ]`, so the count reflects existing owners only and the code is set before the entity is persisted.\n\nThe global sequence behaves as specified: because each new owner is persisted within the same transaction before the next is counted, consecutive creations get consecutive numbers (verified by `coreFormatAndGlobalSequence`: `SMI-000N` then `JON-000(N+1)`).",
